# ADR-002: Transport Layer Choices

## Status

Accepted

## Context

{{.ServiceName}} needs to communicate with external systems. The transport layer must be chosen based on the service's requirements.

## Decision
{{- if .HasHTTP}}

### HTTP (Chi Router)
We use the Chi router for HTTP endpoints. Chi is lightweight, idiomatic, and composable via middleware.
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasGRPC}}

### gRPC (buf)
We use gRPC for service-to-service communication. Proto files are managed with buf for consistency and code generation.
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasKafka}}

### Kafka Consumer
We use Kafka for asynchronous event processing. Consumer groups enable horizontal scaling.
{{- end}}

## Consequences

- All transport handlers live in `adapter/` sub-packages
- Each transport adapter translates between its protocol and domain types
- Business logic remains in `service/` — transport adapters are thin
{{- if .HasHTTP}}
- HTTP middleware handles cross-cutting concerns (auth, CORS, rate limiting)
{{- end}}

